   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "&gt;&gt; On the side note, I had to keep the hacky code e.g. guide_grid_orig &lt;- ggplot2:::guide_grid to be able to display the desired grid style. Is this fixed in 0.91 or is there an alternative way to configure it?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; There is a development branch with the new theming system, and I even think it made it to release candidate status recently (search the devel mailing list for a message from Winston Chang). With the new code on this branch you can control the grid lines of x and y independently.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Instructions for installing the new version:\r<br>  <a href=\"https://github.com/wch/ggplot2/wiki/Installing-the-development-version-of-ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wch/ggplot2/wiki/Installing-the-development-version-of-ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375036547000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ibXIXY0z4R45RyWlr6_Fo\">https://github.com/wch/ggplot2/wiki/Installing-the-development-version-of-ggplot2</a>\r<br>\r<br>And you can get rid of just the horizontal or vertical grid lines with\r<br>something like this:\r<br>  theme(panel.major.x = element_blank(), panel.minor.x = element_blank())\r<br>\r<br>Note that opts() has been replaced by theme() and theme_blank() has\r<br>been replaced by element_blank().\r<br>\r<br>If you&#39;re interested, here is more information about the new theming system:\r<br>  <a href=\"https://github.com/wch/ggplot2/wiki/New-theme-system\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wch/ggplot2/wiki/New-theme-system&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375036547000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3lCyhDoKr7291ARiGZuU4c\">https://github.com/wch/ggplot2/wiki/New-theme-system</a>\r<br>\r<br>-Winston\r<br>"
